{
  "_comment": [
    "M7.1 fixture: the clean two-port wired gateway.",
    "",
    "Two physical Ethernet ports, both connected, one carrying the default",
    "route. This is the shape the canonical profile describes, so it is the",
    "fixture that most directly tests whether M7.1 can recognise a textbook",
    "gateway without also being distracted by infrastructure.",
    "",
    "Both ports report a speed. The LAN candidate deliberately does NOT carry a",
    "default route, because that relationship is what distinguishes it from the",
    "uplink and the analysis must not be able to tell them apart by position."
  ],
